WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.090
If your prep is PEG, this video will walk you through exactly how to take it

2
00:00:04.090 --> 00:00:04.240
.

3
00:00:04.240 --> 00:00:08.720
Just follow along step by step. Your PEG prep is the large container that you'll

4
00:00:08.720 --> 00:00:09.600
mix with water.

5
00:00:09.600 --> 00:00:13.520
You'll also want Crystal Light or flavor packs on hand if you'd like to improve

6
00:00:13.520 --> 00:00:14.000
the taste.

7
00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:18.080
At 8 a.m. the day before your procedure, you'll mix the prep.

8
00:00:18.080 --> 00:00:22.580
Add water to your prep container and stir or shake until everything is fully

9
00:00:22.580 --> 00:00:23.280
dissolved.

10
00:00:23.280 --> 00:00:28.960
Once it's mixed, put it in the refrigerator. Keeping it cold makes it much

11
00:00:28.960 --> 00:00:29.920
easier to drink.

12
00:00:30.560 --> 00:00:35.240
If you're adding Crystal Light or a flavor pack, you can mix that in now. Just

13
00:00:35.240 --> 00:00:36.320
make sure it's

14
00:00:36.320 --> 00:00:42.320
not red, orange, blue, or purple. Stick to clear or light-colored flavors.

15
00:00:42.320 --> 00:00:46.800
Between 4 and 5 p.m. you'll begin drinking the solution.

16
00:00:46.800 --> 00:00:52.000
Here's the pace. Drink 16 ounces, that's about two cups every 30 minutes.

17
00:00:52.000 --> 00:00:56.400
You'll keep going at that pace for about four hours until the entire container

18
00:00:56.400 --> 00:00:57.200
is empty.

19
00:00:57.920 --> 00:01:02.590
Take your time with each glass. Slow, steady sips are easier on your stomach

20
00:01:02.590 --> 00:01:03.040
than trying

21
00:01:03.040 --> 00:01:08.720
to gulp it all at once. This part is really important. You must drink all of

22
00:01:08.720 --> 00:01:09.120
the prep

23
00:01:09.120 --> 00:01:14.000
solution as directed, even if you're already passing clear liquid. I know it

24
00:01:14.000 --> 00:01:14.560
can feel like

25
00:01:14.560 --> 00:01:18.320
enough, but finishing the entire dose is what gives us the clearest view during

26
00:01:18.320 --> 00:01:19.280
your procedure.

27
00:01:19.280 --> 00:01:25.140
If the prep isn't completed as directed, we may need to reschedule, and neither

28
00:01:25.140 --> 00:01:26.000
of us wants that.

29
00:01:26.720 --> 00:01:31.680
Once you've finished, keep drinking clear liquids until bedtime. Staying hydrated will

30
00:01:31.680 --> 00:01:36.080
help you feel better and help the prep do its job. If you experience any

31
00:01:36.080 --> 00:01:36.880
discomfort from

32
00:01:36.880 --> 00:01:41.260
frequent trips to the bathroom, applying a petroleum-based ointment or diaper

33
00:01:41.260 --> 00:01:42.640
rash cream can really help.

34
00:01:42.640 --> 00:01:49.540
That's it. You've got this. Follow the timing, finish the full dose, and stay

35
00:01:49.540 --> 00:01:50.080
hydrated.

36
00:01:51.360 --> 00:01:56.880
If you have any questions at all, don't hesitate to call our office. We're here

37
00:01:56.880 --> 00:01:57.760
to help.
